e is still there, and it will not be printed again.","locale":"en"},"2088":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"**Set your own password**: pass `VNC_PASSWD` at start. The password is rotated only when you change this value, and the new one is printed once.","locale":"en"},"2089":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"If the variable still holds the old public default from earlier docs, the next start treats it as unset and replaces it with a new random password.","locale":"en"},"2090":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"Do not publish `6081` on an untrusted network either.","locale":"en"},"2091":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"Read the current password (it only appears when generated or when you rotate it):","locale":"en"},"2092":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"If a later restart no longer shows it, that is expected — use the value you saved the first time.","locale":"en"},"2093":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are still required.","locale":"en"},"2094":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"SnowLuma's native addon uses `ptrace` to inject the hook into the in-container QQ process. The official image grants `cap_sys_ptrace` to `/usr/local/bin/node`, so SnowLuma can run as the unprivileged `snowluma` user while still injecting within the container's capability boundary.","locale":"en"},"2095":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"With current official images, you no longer need to change the host's `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope`. Keep these container options instead:","locale":"en"},"2096":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"To verify the file capability inside the container:","locale":"en"},"2097":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"If an old image still asks you to relax the host sysctl, upgrade the image first. Changing `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope` should only be a temporary troubleshooting fallback when upgrading is not possible.","locale":"en"},"2098":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **mandatory**. SnowLuma's native addon uses ptrace to inject the hook into the QQ process; the default seccomp profile blocks that.","locale":"en"},"2099":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--shm-size=1g` is needed for QQ's Chromium runtime — the default container `/dev/shm` is too small 