ults to `SNOWLUMA_HOOK_AUTOLOAD=1`: when the container starts, the hook is injected into the QQ process in passive-observe mode. Once you scan-login, the hook auto-promotes to working mode. supervisor also restarts QQ on crash through the same flow."],[2074,"The image does **not** rebuild SnowLuma — it consumes the prebuilt `lite` tarball from each SnowLuma GitHub Release, so the release and the image build are decoupled."],[2036,"The initial WebUI one-time password is available via `docker logs`. BT Panel's container management UI lets you view logs directly."],[1483,"The installer already treats failures per hop: it names the hop that failed and the next action. You can do the same by hand."],[1490,"The installer uses those, then `get.docker.com --mirror Aliyun`"],[1898,"The machine running the MCP client needs `npx` and Node.js `>= 22`."],[2344,"The manual flow is sensitive to your environment. These bits depend heavily on your machine:"],[1945,"The MCP server only calls actions present in the generated catalog. Unknown actions are rejected."],[1690,"The native hook module is loaded via `process.dlopen()`. Source lives in the separate `dev/nnphook` repo."],[2353,"The official host-mode installer splits Xvfb / fluxbox / VNC / noVNC / QQ / SnowLuma into units under `snowluma.target`. Hand-rolling can start with this one wrapper; split later using `templates/host`."],[2086,"The official image has **no** public fixed password. Do not copy sample values from old docs or random posts."],[2313,"The official Linux QQ download page is JS-rendered, so **don't hard-code a version** — grab the current `.deb` for your arch from https\\://im.qq.com/linuxqq/download.html:"],[1721,"The OneBot API reference is generated by the docs repo's `pnpm api:generate` (also wired to `prebuild`) from `docs/public/api/catalog.json` — one page per action, plus a category overview and a searchable landing page. `catalog.json` is the action catalog produced by the main repo's `collectActionDocs